    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "id": "u29.d01.grammar",
      "title": {
        "en": "Reported statements (backshift)",
        "ru": "Косвенная речь (сдвиг времён)"
      },
      "rule": {
        "en": "To report what someone said, use say/tell + (that) and shift the tense back one step: present→past, past→past perfect, will→would, can→could. Also shift pronouns and time words (now→then, tomorrow→the next day).",
        "ru": "Чтобы передать чужие слова: say/tell + (that) и сдвиг времени на шаг назад: настоящее→прошедшее, прошедшее→past perfect, will→would, can→could. Также меняются местоимения и слова времени (now→then, tomorrow→the next day)."
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "present → past",
            "ru": "наст. → прош."
          },
          "formula": "\"I am tired\" → said (that) … was tired",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "He said he was tired.",
              "ru": "Он сказал, что устал."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "past-modals"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "will → would",
            "ru": "will → would"
          },
          "formula": "\"I will help\" → said … would help",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "She said she would help.",
              "ru": "Она сказала, что поможет."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "past-modals"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "say vs tell",
            "ru": "say vs tell"
          },
          "formula": "tell + someone; say + (to sb)",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "He told me he was late.",
              "ru": "Он сказал мне, что опаздывает."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "past-modals"
        }
      ],
      "pitfalls": [
        {
          "en": "\"tell\" needs a person: \"told me\", \"said\" doesn’t: \"said that…\".",
          "ru": "«tell» требует лица: «told me»; «say» — нет: «said that…»."
        },
        {
          "en": "Shift \"will→would\", \"can→could\": \"He said he would come\", not \"will come\".",
          "ru": "Сдвиг «will→would», «can→could»: «He said he would come», не «will come»."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reading",
      "id": "u29.d01.reading",
      "title": {
        "en": "What she told me",
        "ru": "Что она мне рассказала"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "u29.d01.reading.b1",
          "en": "I ran into Mia yesterday and she had a lot to say. She said she had quit her job and was starting a company. She explained that she had been planning it for months and added that she would launch in the spring.",
          "ru": "Вчера я столкнулся с Мией, и ей было что рассказать. Она сказала, что уволилась и открывает компанию. Она объяснила, что планировала это месяцами, и добавила, что запустится весной.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u29.d01.reading.b1.mp3",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "u29.d01.reading.b2",
          "en": "She admitted she was a little scared, but insisted she had never felt more alive. She told me she would need help and promised to call. I said I was happy for her and that I would do anything I could.",
          "ru": "Она призналась, что немного боится, но настаивала, что никогда не чувствовала себя более живой. Она сказала, что ей понадобится помощь, и обещала позвонить. Я сказал, что рад за неё и сделаю всё, что смогу.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u29.d01.reading.b2.mp3",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
